  "name": "Revival Zion and Pukkumina (Jamaican Revivalist worship)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Afro-Christian Revival religion of Jamaica, grown from the Great Revival that swept the island in the mid-nineteenth century, with two branches: Zion, closer to Protestant worship, and Pukkumina (Pocomania), with stronger African retentions. Services set Sankey hymns, sung slow and drawn-out, and fast rhythmic choruses over a bass drum and a rattling side drum with hand clapping, while 'trumping' or 'labouring', a rhythmic over-breathing as worshippers circle, brings on possession by the spirit.",
  "recipe": "classic modern revival zion and pukkumina, ritual Devotional, Afro-diasporic branch. bass snare drum, hand clap. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
